 var descriptions={
 frame:['Crankcase / frame','Supports the main bearings and guides the opposed cylinder assemblies. The teaching cutaway exposes components normally enclosed by solid metal.','Stationary','ariel-kbz'],
 shaft:['Crankshaft and crankpin','The driver rotates the shaft. Each offset crankpin drives a connecting rod, converting rotation into reciprocating motion. The shown throw phasing is illustrative, not a verified installed crankshaft drawing.','Rotating','ariel-kbz'],
 mainbearing:['Main-bearing shell','Supports a main journal and its oil film. The shell stays fixed while the journal rotates inside it. Exact clearance, material specification and installed bearing part number remain unassigned.','Stationary shell / rotating journal','ariel-kbz'],
 conrod:['Connecting rod','The large end follows a crankpin while the small end follows the crosshead. The rod changes angle through the cycle; it does not simply slide as a rigid horizontal link. Generic Ariel connecting-rod length is used for the displayed slider-crank geometry.','Articulating','ariel-kinematics'],
 bigbearing:['Connecting-rod big-end bearing','The bearing shell moves with the connecting rod around the rotating crankpin. Lubrication and correct fit separate the surfaces. This illustration does not calculate bearing loads or clearances.','Orbits with the connecting rod','ariel-kbz'],
 crosshead:['Crosshead','Transfers force from the connecting rod to the piston rod. Its guide keeps piston-rod motion straight while the connecting rod swings.','Reciprocating','ariel-kbz'],
 crosspin:['Crosshead pin and bushing','Forms the articulating joint between connecting rod and crosshead. Alternating load direction helps oil distribution in the retained training discussion; this screen does not calculate rod-reversal margin.','Translates with crosshead; joint articulates','ariel-kbz'],
 shoe:['Crosshead guiding surface','The crosshead guiding surfaces slide along the stationary guide and carry side force from the connecting rod. Geometry represents a teaching interface, not a selected replaceable-shoe design.','Reciprocating with crosshead','ariel-kbz'],
 guide:['Crosshead guide','Keeps the crosshead aligned with the cylinder. Transparent housing is a teaching effect; never operate actual equipment with guards removed to observe motion.','Stationary','ariel-kbz'],
 rod:['Piston rod','Connects the crosshead to the piston through the pressure packing. Its area reduces crank-end swept volume relative to head-end volume. Overall rod length and surface treatment are not assigned from appearance.','Reciprocating','ariel-kinematics'],
 packing:['Rod pressure packing','Stationary packing cups and ring sets seal along the moving rod at the cylinder crank end. Ring arrangement, venting, cooling and lubrication are application-specific; the illustrated stack is representative.','Stationary assembly; rod slides through it','ariel-lube'],
 wiper:['Oil-wiper assembly','Separates frame-oil behavior from the outward-moving rod region. It is not the cylinder gas valve and not a substitute for pressure packing. The drawing represents function, not installed ring selection.','Stationary','ariel-lube'],
 distance:['Distance-piece region','Separates the gas-end packing region from the crankcase/crosshead region. Installed compartment, vent and purge details must come from the exact package records.','Stationary','ariel-lube'],
 piston:['Piston','Reduces the volume at one end of a double-acting cylinder while the other end grows. Both ends have their own suction/discharge valve functions. The model is an ideal cycle, not a measured indicator card.','Reciprocating','ariel-cycle'],
 rings:['Piston sealing-ring set','Limits leakage across the piston between the two cylinder ends. Illustrated groove count, ring splits and material are not a verified bill of materials.','Travels with piston','ariel-rings'],
 wear:['Rider / wear band','Supports and guides the piston within the bore. It has a different function from the gas-sealing ring set. Installed band count and material remain to be verified.','Travels with piston','ariel-rings'],
 barrel:['Cylinder barrel and bore','The pressure-containing cylinder surrounds the piston. Bore proportions use the retained owner-specific source; clearances, wall thickness and cutaway surfaces are teaching geometry.','Stationary','ariel-cycle'],
 head:['Head-end cover and clearance space','Closes the outboard end of the cylinder. Some high-pressure gas remains after discharge and re-expands before fresh gas can enter. The clearance-volume fraction here is explicitly illustrative.','Stationary','ariel-cycle'],
 suction:['Suction check-valve assembly','Opens when cylinder pressure is sufficiently below suction pressure. It closes as compression begins. Lift is enlarged so its plate motion can be seen; exact springs and plate design depend on the installed application.','Pressure-operated plate and spring','ariel-valves'],
 discharge:['Discharge check-valve assembly','Opens when cylinder pressure reaches the discharge-side pressure in the ideal model, and prevents reverse flow during re-expansion. It is not an actuated process shutdown valve.','Pressure-operated plate and spring','ariel-valves'],
 spring:['Valve spring','Returns the valve sealing element toward its seat. Spring number, stiffness, lift and material depend on the selected compressor valve. Animation exaggerates travel and does not model impact or acoustic dynamics.','Compresses and extends with valve lift','ariel-valves'],
 seat:['Valve seat / guard','Provides the flow openings and limits plate travel. The drawn concentric passages are a representative valve construction, not a claim of interchangeability between installed valves.','Stationary','ariel-valves'],
 manifold:['Gas manifold / passage','Shows the teaching gas path associated with the selected bank. Suction and discharge remain separate. Spatial routing and internal galleries are explanatory rather than a fabrication model.','Gas flow only','ariel-cycle'],
 separator:['Interstage liquid separator - schematic','Separates condensed liquid from the interstage gas before the next compression stage. Spatial layout, liquid level and internals here are explanatory; use the retained vendor records for the installed scrubber and its protection.','Gas flow only','ariel-cycle'],
 cooler:['Interstage cooling and liquid separation','Stage-one gas is conditioned before entering the second stage. The simplified cooler/separator symbols explain stage order; this is not a new installed equipment identity or hydraulic route.','Gas flow only','ariel-cycle'],
 lube:['Frame-oil lubrication concept','Oil supports moving frame components through the existing lubrication design. This transparent teaching gallery is not a surveyed drilled passage or an installed feed-rate instruction. Cylinder/packing force-feed is a different duty.','Illustrated oil flow','ariel-lube'],
 pump:['Frame-driven oil-pump gears - schematic','Demonstrates a frame-driven oil supply mechanically separate from process-gas compression. Gear tooth count, internal pump design and speed ratio are representative only. The C-5700 circulation/heater assembly is not reclassified as a cylinder lubricator.','Rotating teaching gears','ariel-lube'],
 pocket:['Clearance-pocket function','Adding effective clearance can reduce fresh-gas intake by extending re-expansion. The inlet source identifies manual VVCP and SVU; residue stage-one records identify FVCP/SVU. This teaching control is not the plant load-step map.','Optional teaching volume change','ariel-cycle'],
 coupling:['Drive coupling','Transmits rotation from the driver to the compressor. No actual machine RPM, driver command or startup is changed by the playback buttons.','Rotating','ariel-kbz']
 };
