 root.innerHTML='<header class="ci-top"><div class="ci-brand"><div class="eyebrow">CLEAR FORK / TRAINING</div><h1>Equipment Internal Training</h1></div><span class="badge">INDEPENDENT TRAINING CLOCK</span><button id="ci-help">Help</button><button id="ci-fullscreen" class="ci-fullscreen">Full screen</button><button id="ci-close" class="danger">Close</button></header><main id="ci-landing" class="ci-landing"><div class="ci-intro"><div class="eyebrow">MECHANISMS / PRESSURE / TEMPERATURE / PHASE</div><h2>Explore how the equipment works.</h2><p class="muted">Choose a representative unit. Explore its moving assembly, follow gas or liquid, and read how pressure, temperature and state change. Playback never starts or changes the live plant.</p></div><div id="ci-cards" class="ci-cards"></div><div class="ci-footnote"><b>Source-aware teaching models.</b> Known unit specifications stay linked to the original records. Internal clearances, timing, valve selection and small construction details are illustrative until verified against serial-specific drawings. Part-number and rating fields are ready for future evidence.</div></main><section id="ci-workspace" class="ci-workspace" hidden><nav class="ci-toolbar"><button id="ci-back">All equipment</button><select id="ci-model" aria-label="Equipment family"></select><button id="ci-toggle-left">Explore</button><button id="ci-toggle-right">Details</button><span class="spacer"></span><span class="toolbar-label ci-mini">Independent of plant controls</span></nav><div class="ci-body"><aside class="ci-left"><div class="ci-view-title"><span class="eyebrow">REPRESENTATIVE UNIT</span><b id="ci-unit-title"></b><small id="ci-unit-subtitle"></small></div><div class="ci-group"><label for="ci-throw">Cylinder / throw</label><select id="ci-throw"></select><label class="ci-check"><input id="ci-isolate" type="checkbox">Focus on this throw</label><button id="ci-focus-cylinder" style="width:100%">Zoom to cylinder</button></div><div class="ci-group"><label for="ci-mode">Housing view</label><select id="ci-mode"><option value="xray">Transparent cutaway</option><option value="internals">Internals only</option><option value="solid">Exterior reference</option></select><label for="ci-opacity" style="margin-top:12px">Shell opacity <output id="ci-opacity-out">12%</output></label><input id="ci-opacity" type="range" min="0" max="45" value="12"><label class="ci-check"><input id="ci-gas" type="checkbox" checked>Gas chambers and flow</label><label class="ci-check"><input id="ci-labels" type="checkbox" checked>Cylinder labels</label><label class="ci-check"><input id="ci-oil" type="checkbox">Lubrication and tubing</label><label for="ci-oil-circuit">Lubrication circuit</label><select id="ci-oil-circuit"><option value="all">All circuits</option><option value="frame">Circulating frame oil</option><option value="forcefeed">Cylinder / packing force-feed</option><option value="drain">Packing vent / drain boundaries</option></select><label class="ci-check"><input id="ci-oil-only" type="checkbox">Isolate oil systems</label><button id="ci-oil-view" style="width:100%">Oil-system view</button></div><div class="ci-group"><label for="ci-demo">Selected-throw lesson</label><select id="ci-demo"><option value="loaded">Loaded cycle</option><option value="clearance">Extra head-end clearance</option><option value="unload">Head-end suction held open</option></select><p class="ci-mini">Concept demonstration only. Not a plant load-step command, approved unloading order or installed clearance setting.</p></div><div class="ci-group"><label for="ci-search">Find an illustrated part</label><input id="ci-search" type="search" placeholder="Piston, packing, valve..."><div id="ci-parts" class="ci-parts" style="margin-top:8px"></div><p id="ci-part-count" class="ci-mini"></p><button id="ci-export" style="width:100%">Export parts worksheet</button></div></aside><div class="ci-center" id="ci-stage"><canvas id="ci-canvas" tabindex="0" aria-label="Interactive equipment cutaway. Drag to orbit, wheel to zoom, click to identify a part."></canvas><canvas id="ci-overlay" aria-hidden="true"></canvas><div class="ci-canvas-tools"><div class="ci-purpose12mt" role="group" aria-label="Choose how to explore"><button data-purpose="flow">Learn the flow</button><button data-purpose="mechanism">Moving parts</button><button data-purpose="oil">Oil and support</button></div><details class="ci-camera12mt"><summary>Camera views</summary><div><button data-view="overview">Reset view</button><button data-view="top">Top</button><button data-view="drive">Drive end</button><button data-view="side">Section</button><button id="ci-focus-part">Focus selection</button></div></details></div><div id="ci-selection12mt" class="ci-selection12mt" role="status">Choose a view above, then select a part.</div><div class="ci-orbit-hint" id="ci-hint">Drag: orbit &nbsp; | &nbsp; Right-drag / Shift-drag: pan &nbsp; | &nbsp; Wheel / pinch: zoom &nbsp; | &nbsp; Click: identify</div><div class="ci-renderer" id="ci-renderer"></div></div><aside class="ci-right"><div class="ci-tabs" role="tablist"><button data-tab="component" class="active" role="tab" aria-selected="true">Component</button><button data-tab="specs" role="tab" aria-selected="false">Unit info</button><button data-tab="coverage" role="tab" aria-selected="false">Coverage</button><button data-tab="sources" role="tab" aria-selected="false">Sources</button></div><div id="ci-panel" class="ci-panel"></div></aside></div><footer class="ci-playback"><div class="ci-timeline"><label for="ci-timeline">Crank angle</label><input id="ci-timeline" aria-label="Crank angle" type="range" min="0" max="360" step=".5" value="34.5"><output id="ci-angle">34.5 deg</output><span id="ci-cycle-label" class="ci-mini">Ideal cycle</span></div><div class="ci-transport"><button id="ci-step-back" title="Back 5 degrees">-5<span class="step-label"> deg</span></button><button id="ci-rewind">Rewind</button><button id="ci-play" class="primary">Play</button><button id="ci-pause">Pause</button><button id="ci-forward">Forward 2x</button><button id="ci-step-forward" title="Forward 5 degrees">+5<span class="step-label"> deg</span></button><select id="ci-speed" aria-label="Teaching playback speed"><option value=".25">0.25x</option><option value=".5">0.5x</option><option value="1" selected>1x</option><option value="2">2x</option></select><span class="state" id="ci-state">PAUSED / TEACHING SPEED</span></div><div class="ci-flow-strip" id="ci-flow"></div></footer></section><div id="ci-toast" class="ci-toast" hidden role="status"></div><div id="ci-help-modal" class="ci-help" hidden role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="Training navigation help"><article><h2>Explore at your own pace.</h2><p><b>Play</b> moves the private training timeline forward. <b>Pause</b> freezes it. <b>Rewind</b> reviews earlier cycle states; it does not mean running a compressor backward. <b>Forward 2x</b> reviews more quickly. Drag the angle slider or step by 5 degrees to examine piston/valve timing or the Frick working-pocket cycle.</p><p><b>Mouse:</b> drag to orbit; wheel to zoom; right-drag or Shift-drag to pan. <b>Touch:</b> one finger orbits; two fingers pan and pinch to zoom. Click/tap a visible solid internal part to identify it, or select it from the part list. Transparent shells do not block picking internal parts.</p><p><b>Views:</b> Overview resets the camera. Cylinder section isolates a reciprocating throw; Rotor section and the assembly selector isolate Frick subassemblies. Focus part centers your selected component. Explore and Details collapse the side panels so the model can fill the screen.</p><p><b>Keys:</b> Space plays/pauses; Left/Right step 5 degrees; Home resets the view; F focuses; Escape closes this help, then returns to the plant. Keys typed into controls never reach the plant.</p><p><b>Evidence:</b> Unit info reads the exact representative records and preserves current corrections and historical qualifications. Reciprocating P-V pressure, valve lift and clearance are educational. The Frick graph shows normalized working-pocket volume, not calculated propane pressure or refrigeration capacity. Process explains pressure, temperature and phase; P/Ps and T/Ts use absolute-scale normalized teaching ratios. Pump scenarios distinguish normal liquid from abnormal vapor formation. Flow X-ray uses a projection overlay, not an occlusion-accurate fluid simulation. No operating setpoints, part numbers or ratings are inferred from this cutaway.</p><p><b>Display:</b> Native WebGL is preferred. A perspective Canvas 3D fallback uses the same geometry and picking when WebGL is unavailable; rendering speed depends on the device. No heavy model is built until you choose a unit.</p><button id="ci-help-close" class="primary">Return to trainer</button></article></div>';
